# Copy to .env next to compose.yaml on all four boxes, the same file on each. Compose passes every line into the
# container, where the gr8 launcher reads it as an option. Unset lines take the launcher's default (./gr8 knobs).

# --- the model (pinned to the commits measured in README.md) -----------------------------------------------------------
GR8_MODEL=glm53
# Release v0.7 (the mul1 weights) — the release the v3 rows were measured on (README "What is new in v3").
MODEL=https://huggingface.co/kindlingai/glm-5.3-exlr8-k2-k3-k4@9e25c28a2e8808d8b2599d780521fd6af24e7558
# glm53 at TP=4 drafts with the DFlash2 drafter (gr8 docs/DEPLOY.md). Its licence is CC BY-NC-ND 4.0: it forbids
# sharing a converted copy, so EACH BOX downloads the drafter and converts its own rank part (./fetch, ./gr8 prepare).
# Pinned like MODEL (see incoai/GLM-5.3-DFlash2@425aa61...); drop the @<commit> to follow the repo's main.
DRAFTER=https://huggingface.co/incoai/GLM-5.3-DFlash2@425aa615ce320caac34400208b30808c8f14f76c
# The width manifest: bit280 (the v3 default — KindlingAI's own v0.7 profile, about 2.80 routed bits per
# weight, shipped in manifests/), bit275 (the v2 default), home, bit325, bit338, up1, bit225, bit243, bit260,
# down1, or a path to a custom exlr8-v2-manifest JSON. ./gr8 knobs VARIANT says what each shipped one is.
#VARIANT=bit280
# Sent only to Hugging Face, for a gated or private repo.
#HF_TOKEN=

# --- the four boxes ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Placeholders: put THIS cluster's addresses in. The 10G LAN address of every box, in rank order, head first; the head
# serves the OpenAI API on port 8100. TP is the number of addresses.
PEERS=192.0.2.1,192.0.2.2,192.0.2.3,192.0.2.4
TP=4
# Each box's ConnectX address on PCIe root 1 (IPS) and PCIe root 2 (IPS2), in PEERS order. Unset, the boxes find each other through mentat, or use one NIC per rail's default.
IPS=10.0.0.1,10.0.0.2,10.0.0.3,10.0.0.4
IPS2=10.0.1.1,10.0.1.2,10.0.1.3,10.0.1.4
# No switch: the boxes are cabled in a ring, in PEERS cable order; leave out IPS and IPS2.
#SHAPE=ring

# --- the knobs (README.md, "Pick what to prioritize") -------------------------------------------------------------------
# What to prioritize: quality (the default, measured), speed, context, agents or agents-fast (knobs.sh; agents = quality
# with SHARE_LIMIT=16384, measured 2026-11-09; agents-fast = agents + GR8_REUSE_ALIGN=0, opt-in, NOT bit-exact against a
# cold prefill). The speed slot was removed: its two measured knobs were no gain (knobs 3-5 cancelled).
#TUNE=quality
# The requests that decode at once. Unset: 8, gr8's TP=4 default. The concurrency floor for a winning config is SESS>=4.
#SESS=8
# The concurrency dial: CONC=1|2|4|6|8 sets SESS and lets CAP follow the largest CAP a boot at that SESS measured
# holding the serving floor (conc.tsv header) — fewer slots, more KV cache per
# session. Unset: the recipe default CONC=8 (the serving choice; the measured bit280 row: 8 sessions at the
# 1,048,576-token pool, attic on, one boot 2026-11-21 (v3.2, gr8 97089b3); ./glm53 conc prints the table for the current VARIANT).
# A CAP you set keeps your value (one above the measured value warns on ./glm53 up). A pair with no measured
# row falls back to SESS=CONC and this TUNE's CAP, with a stderr line.
#CONC=8
# The memory-reserve layer (spark-attic, github.com/bertholomus/spark-attic): ATTIC=1 boots with
# compose.attic.yaml (the layer lends each rank its display-carveout slice, so the CONC rows with attic on
# hold a bigger pool) and needs GR8_IMAGE to name an image WITH the attic client — the attic client is NOT in
# a published gr8 image, so the default GR8_IMAGE below names a build you make (the pinned stock gr8 97089b3
# plus the attic client; README "The memory-reserve layer"). ATTIC=0 boots the pinned stock image instead — the
# v3-v3.2 bit280 rows were measured with the layer ON; attic-off rows are not measured on bit280. Default 1 (the
# measured lane).
ATTIC=1
# The KV pool in tokens, shared by the sessions. Unset: the CONC dial's measured row (1,048,576 at CONC=8 attic
# on, bit280); TUNE=context sets 513536 (KV_FORMAT=int4).
#CAP=1048576
# The KV format: every tier sets it explicitly (v2.1, issue #1) — fp8, except TUNE=context (int4, CAP 513536).
# Leave it unset to take the tier value; set KV_FORMAT=fp8 to roll any tier back to fp8.
#KV_FORMAT=fp8
# 0: the boxes in PEERS. 1: find the boxes through the host's mentat daemon, in group GROUP.
#MENTAT=0
#GROUP=gr8-glm53-4x
# The busy guard (README, "The busy guard"): BUSY=1 refuses a request that would evict a retained session KV
# (HTTP 429 + Retry-After) instead of evicting it or queueing it in silence. The guard ships in stock gr8
# (v2.1, PR #516), so the pinned image carries it and BUSY=1 needs no custom build. Recipe defaults when
# BUSY=1: BUSY_IDLE_SECS 60, BUSY_RETRY_AFTER 60, BUSY_QUEUE_MAX 8 — gr8's own upstream values, the pair the
# measured lane runs. A retry at or above the idle bound can lose an obedient client's own run (README); an
# agent lane that obeys Retry-After should set BUSY_IDLE_SECS=120 BUSY_RETRY_AFTER=20.
BUSY=1

# --- The SSD KV store (on by default in v3; README "Switching and the SSD KV store") --------------------------------------
# At an orderly stop the engine writes the chats it holds to the store; the next boot reads the index back, so a
# chat's next turn restores its KV instead of a prefill. GR8_STOP_GRACE gives docker's stop the time that write
# needs (compose.yaml reads it for stop_grace_period): without it docker kills the engine mid-store. keep=all
# stores every session; the measured cost (141.8-146.4 GB/h a box writes under load, one boot 2026-11-19) and
# the honest base note (the store is Chuck's (@ck2084 on X; GitHub @chuck-ads / @adapt-ai-systems, KindlingAI)
# gr8 #484/#498/#500/#501) are in the README. Comment BOTH lines out to turn the tier off.
KV_STORE=ssd:/var/lib/gr8/home/kv,size=200G,persist=on,keep=all
GR8_STOP_GRACE=150s

# --- faster restarts and engine knobs ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GR8_GEN_CACHE: the loader keeps the tensors it computes at load on this box's disk and reads them back at the next
# boot of the same image (SWITCHING.md). The first boot of an image writes it.
#
# UPDATE 2 (Kindling, 2026-11-07, verified on this rig): GR8_* engine knobs reach the engine ONLY through EXTRA_ENV.
# A plain GR8_FOO=... line in .env is dropped by the launcher (a -e GR8_MOE_TOPK=6 never reached engine.env; a
# -e EXTRA_ENV=GR8_MOE_TOPK=6 did). Append new GR8_* knobs to this ONE line, space-separated NAME=value, and never
# replace what is already here. Short launcher names (SESS, CAP, KV_FORMAT, KVB, ...) stay plain lines above.
# The v3 serving words (the measured lane's values, 2026-11-19): GR8_GEN_CACHE below, GR8_QUIT_FAST=1 (a
# SIGTERM'd engine quits without draining), GR8_S2_DECODE_PF=4096 and GR8_S2_DECODE_ROUNDS=2 (S2 decode paging).
EXTRA_ENV=GR8_GEN_CACHE=/var/lib/gr8/cache/gen GR8_QUIT_FAST=1 GR8_S2_DECODE_PF=4096 GR8_S2_DECODE_ROUNDS=2

# --- the serving knobs (plain launcher options; the measured v3 lane's values) ---------------------------------------------
# KVB=fp8: the KV bridge format. CP_ONECHAIN=1: one chain per rank in the KV bridge. S2_SHARED_WATERFILL=1: the
# S2 scheduler shares decode steps across sessions. KV_WRITE_LIMIT=0.5: the SSD store writes at most half the
# box's disk bandwidth (README "Switching and the SSD KV store").
KVB=fp8
CP_ONECHAIN=1
S2_SHARED_WATERFILL=1
KV_WRITE_LIMIT=0.5

# --- the image (read by compose, not the launcher) -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# The v3.2 default lane runs ATTIC=1, so GR8_IMAGE names a gr8 build WITH the attic client: the pinned stock
# image ghcr.io/kindlingai/gr8:sha-97089b3@sha256:717168f9afff1538c49383502e662fb45bd34d23630ac00f4d88fb1502b2fe4c
# (gr8 97089b3, after KindlingAI's v1.1.0 — the build the v3.2 row was measured on) plus the attic client (spark-attic;
# NOT in any published gr8 image) — build it and tag it gr8:97089b3-attic (README "The memory-reserve layer"). With
# ATTIC=0, set the stock pin itself:
#GR8_IMAGE=ghcr.io/kindlingai/gr8:sha-97089b3@sha256:717168f9afff1538c49383502e662fb45bd34d23630ac00f4d88fb1502b2fe4c
GR8_IMAGE=gr8:97089b3-attic
# A host directory for this box's part of the release (~90 GB at TP=4), owned by uid 1000, in place of the cache volume.
#GR8_CACHE=/srv/glm53/cache
# A host directory for logs and state (out/, s2/, run/), owned by uid 1000, in place of the home volume.
#GR8_HOME=/srv/glm53/home

# --- other ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files the fetch takes at once (gr8's downloader).
#FETCH_JOBS=8
# Any other gr8 launcher option (gr8/KNOBS.md) works here too, as NAME=VALUE. Engine settings ride EXTRA_ENV (above).
